iversal bound of 2 for the nuclear dimension of every graph C*-algebra, and Theorem A computes the exact value, 0 or 1, for every graph with no path from an isolated cycle to another cycle — the class covering Condition (K).\nSecond, both main theorems run through Corollary 3.4, whose decisive inputs are two unpublished preprints: Theorems 3.1 and Proposition 3.3 are imported from Carrión–Gabe–Schafhauser–Tikuisis–White's \"Classifying *-homomorphisms II,\" and Theorem 3.2 invokes Szabó's KK-uniqueness theorem, currently arXiv-only. As written, the main results are conditional on those imports, not defective in their internal logic.\n\nWhat's actually new: Theorem B fills a real gap — [26] had ≤2 only under Condition (K), Ruiz–Sims–Tomforde covered purely infinite algebras, and no universal finite bound was known for arbitrary graphs. Theorem A's exact formula is new. The faithful nuclear dimension invariant is a genuine addition: it is computable for C(X), Z-stable simple algebras, and O∞-stable algebras, and it threads the known extension results — Brake–Winter's Toeplitz computation, the Cuntz–Toeplitz result, and [24, 25, 30] — through one framework. The paper is honest where it counts: the two smallest unresolved graphs are shown, the C(T)⊗K \"+1\" obstruction is named, and the reduction from arbitrary graphs to finite ones is careful, including the check that the Drinen–Tomforde desingularization preserves the isolated-cycle condition.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nThe Graded Classification Conjecture holds for graphs with disjoint cycles | alphaXiv (https://www.alphaxiv.org/es/abs/2505.16706)\nciteturn6search3 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.5 years ago; Crawled: 6 days ago; The Graded Classification Conjecture (GCC) states that the pointed $K_0^{\\operatorname{gr}}$K 0 gr​-group is a complete invariant of the Leavitt path algebras of finite graphs when these algebras are considered with their natural grad